# FCP — Federated Commerce Protocol

**The problem:** Every AI agent that wants to complete a purchase has to build a custom integration with every merchant. Every merchant has to support every agent separately. The result is an N×N integration problem that fragments agentic commerce before it can scale.

**What FCP does:** FCP defines a single common language — a set of open, vendor-neutral APIs — that any agent can speak and any merchant can implement once. A merchant who adopts FCP is instantly reachable by every FCP-compatible agent, without custom builds.

**Where it goes further than existing protocols:** FCP normalises the strongest ideas from UCP, ACP (OpenAI/Stripe), and AP2 (Google) into one spec. It adds a cryptographic mandate chain — three linked digital contracts (IntentMandate → CartMandate → SettlementMandate) — that prove a real user authorised a specific agent to spend a specific amount at a specific merchant. Payment tokens never pass through the agent. Fraud signals, device identity, and location context travel with every call.

**The outcome:** Merchants plug in once and reach all agents. Agents integrate once and reach all merchants. Users get secure, auditable, non-repudiable transactions regardless of which AI surface they shop through.

